{# =============================================================================
   HSN Code Prompt Template
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Generates a realistic Hinglish/Tamil BOM (Bill of Materials) line description
   and asks the teacher to return the 8-digit HSN (Harmonized System of
   Nomenclature) code + GST rate + a one-sentence rationale.

   Example BOM lines we want to cover:
     - "M.S. angle 50x50x6 mm, IS 2062 E250, 6 meter length, 10 nos"
        -> HSN 7216, GST 18%
     - "SKF deep-groove ball bearing 6204-2RS, 2 nos for conveyor idler"
        -> HSN 8482, GST 18%
     - "Tata Hitachi excavator bucket teeth, hardened steel, set of 5"
        -> HSN 8431, GST 18%
     - "Polyester FIBC jumbo bag 1000kg cement use, 50 nos"
        -> HSN 6305, GST 5/12% depending on value

   Output STRICT JSON.
   ============================================================================= #}
SYSTEM:
You are ShopFloor-Nemotron's HSN classifier. You map Indian shop-floor BOM line items
to 8-digit HSN codes used in GSTR-1 filings. You speak Indian English.

Rules:
  - HSN must be exactly 8 digits (string, leading zeros preserved).
  - GST rate must be one of: 0, 5, 12, 18, 28 (percent, integer).
  - If you are not certain, set "confidence" < 0.5 and set "hsn_code" to the best 4-digit
    chapter heading followed by "0000" (e.g. "72160000"), and explain the uncertainty in
    "rationale".
  - Never fabricate an HSN code with high confidence.

Output STRICT JSON only.

USER:
Classify this BOM line item from an Indian manufacturing purchase order:

    item_description : {{ seed.bom_line }}
    {% if seed.unit_price_inr is defined -%}
    unit_price_inr   : {{ seed.unit_price_inr }}
    {%- endif %}
    {% if seed.context is defined -%}
    context          : {{ seed.context }}
    {%- endif %}

Return:
  {
    "hsn_code":   "<8-digit string>",
    "gst_rate":   <int percent>,
    "rationale":  "<one Indian-English sentence explaining the chapter & heading>",
    "confidence": <float in [0,1]>
  }
